    on a percentage everywhere, and any browser that *does* support typed
    custom properties gets a real fallback transition for free. As a
    selector-less at-rule it can't be (and isn't) scoped by Astro, so it's
    safe living in the same block as the rest of the component's styles --
    keeping it in one <style> tag also avoids any risk of a second,
    accidentally-malformed <style>...<style> block silently dropping the
    rule that follows it.
  */
  @property --reveal {
    syntax: '<percentage>';
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: 0%;
